# Most model assets stay OUT of git-lfs on purpose: a plain `git clone` has to
# produce a runnable project on a machine that has nothing but git and Godot
# installed. With an lfs filter those files would check out as ~134-byte pointer
# text instead of geometry, Godot's ufbx importer would fail with "Unrecognized
# file format", and the weapon viewmodel would silently end up with no mesh.
#
# The one exception is the parking map assembly.glb (~230 MB): it is too large
# for GitHub's 100 MB plain-blob push limit, so it MUST go through git-lfs.
# Cloning that map correctly therefore requires `git lfs install` + `git lfs pull`
# (or a clone on a machine with git-lfs configured). Without git-lfs the parking
# map — and only that map — checks out as a pointer and will not import.
*.glb binary
*.fbx binary
*.gltf -text
*.bin binary
assets/environment/parking_rework/assembly.glb filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
